---
description: Run the installed accessibility audit plugin without changing the target project's source or governance.
alwaysApply: false
---

For an accessibility audit, call `run_accessibility_audit` once. Confirm the pages/input and auditor before execution. Use `Automated` as the editable default and do not re-ask for information already present in a page list.

Treat the target repository as read-only. Do not install into, edit, lint, format, build, or test its source. Do not modify governance, agent rules, CI, hooks, manifests, or lockfiles. Write only to the configured audit output directory.

Run authorized pages at desktop, mobile, and 320px reflow headlessly. If no supported browser is available, allow the plugin to install Playwright Chromium once in plugin-owned storage after confirmation. Dismiss visible consent banners before interaction checks and evidence capture. If one remains blocking, report it and skip underlying interaction checks. Keep contextual component screenshots enabled and retain at most one representative image per final confirmed, blocker, or review reporting unit when capture succeeds; use full-page screenshots only for page-level failures or unresolved blockers. Surface progress and allow graceful cancellation to finish writing, packaging, and validating partial output.

Treat only deterministic reproduced failures as confirmed. Keep two-source 404/410 or missing fragments separate from placeholder/5xx review items. Do not treat optional tab Home/End behavior as a failure. Do not require an ordinary disclosure or accordion to close with Escape, and do not report missing aria-controls alone. Use one row only for repeated instances of the same component/root cause. Keep distinct colour treatments, implementations, behaviours, criteria, remediation requirements, and page-specific findings separate. Retain related axe nodes, interaction blockers, truncation/incomplete metadata, unresolved focus samples, incomplete interactions, and the JSON coverage matrix. Keep indeterminate signals in JSON/inconclusive coverage instead of promoting them to workbook findings. Notes contain concrete fixes only.
